title: The Arms Count
subtitle: The hundreds have more men than rifles.
view-if: crisis_october = 1 and e23_rising_phase = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.octTick(Q.crisis_time + 1);
Q.e23_raid_ok = 0;
!}
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Arms Count

The military apparatus has counted the party's weapons for the plan: [+ e23_oct_arms_words +], some machine guns from 1920, pistols, and hand grenades of uncertain age. The Russian officers say a rising needs four times as many. The Reichswehr and the Black Reichswehr have stores all over Germany, and some of them are badly guarded.

- @raid: Raid a Reichswehr depot.
- @buy: Buy rifles through Moscow's agents.
- @police: Empty the Saxon police armouries.

@raid
subtitle: The apparatus thinks it is about even. If it fails, the Reichswehr learns where to look.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_raid_ok = Math.random() < 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e23_raid_ok) {
    Q.e23_oct_arms += 4;
} else {
    Q.e23_oct_arms = Math.max(0, Q.e23_oct_arms - 1);
    RG.district('halle', {repression: 8, guards: -0.5});
}
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

[? if e23_raid_ok = 1 : At night the hundreds take a Black Reichswehr store outside Halle. Two of ours are killed and four thousand rifles change hands. ?][? if e23_raid_ok = 0 : The guards were waiting. Three of ours are killed at the gate, and the next morning the police search every allotment in Merseburg. ?]

@buy
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Russian money, Dutch smugglers and a barge on the Elbe.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no money.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e23_oct_arms += 3;
Q.independence -= 2;
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

Most of the crates arrive. One holds Mexican saddles.

@police
subtitle: Our minister signs the order. Müller will treat it as mutiny.
view-if: e23_saxon_police = 1 and e23_armoury_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_armoury_done = 1;
Q.e23_oct_arms += 6;
Q.army_loyalty += 3;
RG.district('saxony', {guards: 2});
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

Lorries from the hundreds load the police rifles in Dresden and Leipzig under the eyes of the police officers who are supposed to guard them.
